    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11643" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crĭtĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κριτικός</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>fit</i> or <i>suitable for deciding,
				capable of judging.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Adj., only as a medic. t. t. (cf. crisimus), <i>decisive, critical</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">accessio morbi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Conf. 6, 1 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—More frequent, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crĭtĭ-cus</span></b> , i,
				m., <i>a critic</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				9, 10, 1</span></i> (also ap. <i><span class="en">Suet. Gram. 14</span></i>); <i><span class="en">Quint. 2, 1,
				4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 2, 1,
		51</span></i>.</div>
